; The codepoint walk, in one stdlib-only library: [seekwright.text], wrapped as
; [Seekwright_text], the way [lib/providers/] is [seekwright.providers] and
; [lib/fetch/] is [seekwright.fetch].
;
; It exists because the same walk had five copies in this tree, in three
; spellings of the same byte test, and the engine's copy was the one that did not
; clamp its slice — which raised out of a value-typed module
; (plans/reviews/2026-11-12-style-review.md, H1 and H2). A module inside [lib/]
; could not be that owner: [seekwright] cannot be linked by [seekwright.fetch]
; (the direction both dune files state), and [seekwright.fetch] cannot be linked
; by [seekwright], so every module on both sides re-wrote it.
;
; [seekwright] and [seekwright.fetch] both link this, and nothing here links
; either: no wire model, no page record, no fetch backend, no grant. That is what
; keeps the recorded direction intact — [mcp-caps → seekwright →
; seekwright.providers / seekwright.fetch] — with one stdlib-only floor under it.
; It is also why [lib/caps/error.ml] keeps its own byte-backing helper: [mcp-caps]
; may not depend on a seekwright library, and this one carries the [seekwright.]
; prefix.
(library
 (name seekwright_text)
 (public_name seekwright.text))
